{"id":"32927f4e222d9c70","group":"58","path":"58/batch03/58-df-heegner-point.md","title":"Heegner Point","display":"df-heegner-point — Heegner Point","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-heegner-point","aliases":["58-df-heegner-point"],"display":"df-heegner-point — Heegner Point","depends_on":["[[58-df-elliptic-curve]]","[[58-df-modular-curve]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-heegner-point"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-heegner-point</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-heegner-point — Heegner Point"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"74f4744df7db749f\" href=\"?note=74f4744df7db749f\" title=\"58-df-elliptic-curve\">58-df-elliptic-curve</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"e1616e874e8eb33c\" href=\"?note=e1616e874e8eb33c\" title=\"58-df-modular-curve\">58-df-modular-curve</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"E,K,N,\\mathcal O,\\varphi,P,x\\in V\">\\(E,K,N,\\mathcal O,\\varphi,P,x\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{EllipticCurve}_S:V^4\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{EllipticCurve}_S:V^4\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span>, with parameter order <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(E,k,O,K_E)\">\\((E,k,O,K_E)\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"74f4744df7db749f\" href=\"?note=74f4744df7db749f\" title=\"58-df-elliptic-curve\">58-df-elliptic-curve</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X_0(N)\">\\(X_0(N)\\)</span> denotes the modular curve supplied by the orbit presentation in <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"e1616e874e8eb33c\" href=\"?note=e1616e874e8eb33c\" title=\"58-df-modular-curve\">58-df-modular-curve</a>.</li>\n<li>Imaginary quadratic fields, orders, splitting of rational primes, ring-class fields, algebraic-curve morphisms, and rational points are kept at the metatheoretic arithmetic-geometry layer here.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{RationalPrime}_{\\mathsf{meta}}\">\\(\\operatorname{RationalPrime}_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Splits}_{\\mathsf{meta}}\">\\(\\operatorname{Splits}_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\)</span> denote the usual arithmetic predicates.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ImaginaryQuadratic}_{\\mathsf{meta}}\">\\(\\operatorname{ImaginaryQuadratic}_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{HeegnerHypothesis}_{\\mathsf{meta}}\">\\(\\operatorname{HeegnerHypothesis}_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Order}_{\\mathsf{meta}}\">\\(\\operatorname{Order}_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ModularParametrization}_{\\mathsf{meta}}\">\\(\\operatorname{ModularParametrization}_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{CMPoint}_{\\mathsf{meta}}\">\\(\\operatorname{CMPoint}_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{HeegnerPointData}_{\\mathsf{meta}}\">\\(\\operatorname{HeegnerPointData}_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\)</span> are the metatheoretic relations used below.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{HeegnerPoint}_S(P,E,K)\">\\(\\mathrm{HeegnerPoint}_S(P,E,K)\\)</span> is retained only as a metasyntactic compatibility name for downstream atoms.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}heegner\\text{-}point\\text{-}hypothesis}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\operatorname{HeegnerHypothesis}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(K,N)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{ImaginaryQuadratic}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(K)\n\\land N\\in\\mathbb N_{&gt;0}\n\\land\\forall\\ell\\in\\mathbb N\\;\\Bigl(\n(\\operatorname{RationalPrime}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\ell)\\land\\ell\\mid N)\n\\to\\operatorname{Splits}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\ell,K)\\Bigr).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}heegner\\text{-}point\\text{-}hypothesis}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\operatorname{HeegnerHypothesis}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(K,N)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{ImaginaryQuadratic}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(K)\n\\land N\\in\\mathbb N_{&gt;0}\n\\land\\forall\\ell\\in\\mathbb N\\;\\Bigl(\n(\\operatorname{RationalPrime}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\ell)\\land\\ell\\mid N)\n\\to\\operatorname{Splits}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\ell,K)\\Bigr).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}heegner\\text{-}point\\text{-}data}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\operatorname{HeegnerPointData}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(P,E,K,N,\\mathcal O,\\varphi,x)\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\exists O,K_E\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{EllipticCurve}_S(E,\\mathbb Q,O,K_E)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\operatorname{HeegnerHypothesis}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(K,N)\n\\land\\operatorname{Order}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\mathcal O,K)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\gcd(N,[\\mathcal O_K:\\mathcal O])=1\n\\land\\operatorname{ModularParametrization}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\varphi,X_0(N),E,O)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\operatorname{CMPoint}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(x,X_0(N),\\mathcal O)\n\\land P=\\varphi(x)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}heegner\\text{-}point\\text{-}data}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\operatorname{HeegnerPointData}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(P,E,K,N,\\mathcal O,\\varphi,x)\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\exists O,K_E\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{EllipticCurve}_S(E,\\mathbb Q,O,K_E)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\operatorname{HeegnerHypothesis}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(K,N)\n\\land\\operatorname{Order}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\mathcal O,K)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\gcd(N,[\\mathcal O_K:\\mathcal O])=1\n\\land\\operatorname{ModularParametrization}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\varphi,X_0(N),E,O)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\operatorname{CMPoint}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(x,X_0(N),\\mathcal O)\n\\land P=\\varphi(x)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}heegner\\text{-}point\\text{-}existential}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\operatorname{HeegnerPoint}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(P,E,K)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists N,\\mathcal O,\\varphi,x\\;\\operatorname{HeegnerPointData}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(P,E,K,N,\\mathcal O,\\varphi,x).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}heegner\\text{-}point\\text{-}existential}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\operatorname{HeegnerPoint}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(P,E,K)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists N,\\mathcal O,\\varphi,x\\;\\operatorname{HeegnerPointData}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(P,E,K,N,\\mathcal O,\\varphi,x).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}heegner\\text{-}point\\text{-}compatibility}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\mathrm{HeegnerPoint}_S(P,E,K)\n\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{HeegnerPoint}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(P,E,K).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}heegner\\text{-}point\\text{-}compatibility}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\mathrm{HeegnerPoint}_S(P,E,K)\n\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{HeegnerPoint}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(P,E,K).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The previous formula mixed set predicates with uncoded schemes, rational-point functors, discriminants, and class fields. The corrected atom exposes that arithmetic-geometry boundary and no longer claims those constructions are defined set-level primitives.</li>\n<li>The exact four-place elliptic-curve source is used, with base field <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb Q\">\\(\\mathbb Q\\)</span> and its presentation witnesses explicitly quantified.</li>\n<li>The target elliptic curve need not have complex multiplication. The CM datum belongs to the source point on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X_0(N)\">\\(X_0(N)\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Gross–Zagier relates the height of a suitable Heegner point to <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L&#39;(E/K,1)\">\\(L&#39;(E/K,1)\\)</span> under appropriate hypotheses.</li>\n<li>Gross–Zagier (1986): <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L&#39;(E, 1)\">\\(L&#39;(E, 1)\\)</span> relates to the height of Heegner points.</li>\n<li>Kolyvagin: Heegner points <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\to\">\\(\\to\\)</span> Mordell–Weil group.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-elliptic-curve","status":"resolved","id":"74f4744df7db749f","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-elliptic-curve]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-modular-curve","status":"resolved","id":"e1616e874e8eb33c","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-modular-curve]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-elliptic-curve","status":"resolved","id":"74f4744df7db749f","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{EllipticCurve}_S:V^4\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}$, with parameter order $(E,k,O,K_E)$ (see [[58-df-elliptic-curve]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-modular-curve","status":"resolved","id":"e1616e874e8eb33c","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$X_0(N)$ denotes the modular curve supplied by the orbit presentation in [[58-df-modular-curve]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"E,K,N,\\mathcal O,\\varphi,P,x\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{EllipticCurve}_S:V^4\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"(E,k,O,K_E)","display":false},{"tex":"X_0(N)","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{RationalPrime}_{\\mathsf{meta}}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Splits}_{\\mathsf{meta}}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{ImaginaryQuadratic}_{\\mathsf{meta}}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{HeegnerHypothesis}_{\\mathsf{meta}}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Order}_{\\mathsf{meta}}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{ModularParametrization}_{\\mathsf{meta}}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{CMPoint}_{\\mathsf{meta}}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{HeegnerPointData}_{\\mathsf{meta}}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{HeegnerPoint}_S(P,E,K)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}heegner\\text{-}point\\text{-}hypothesis}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\operatorname{HeegnerHypothesis}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(K,N)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{ImaginaryQuadratic}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(K)\n\\land N\\in\\mathbb N_{>0}\n\\land\\forall\\ell\\in\\mathbb N\\;\\Bigl(\n(\\operatorname{RationalPrime}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\ell)\\land\\ell\\mid N)\n\\to\\operatorname{Splits}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\ell,K)\\Bigr).","display":true},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}heegner\\text{-}point\\text{-}data}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\operatorname{HeegnerPointData}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(P,E,K,N,\\mathcal O,\\varphi,x)\n\\leftrightarrow{}&\n\\exists O,K_E\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{EllipticCurve}_S(E,\\mathbb Q,O,K_E)\\\\\n&\\land\\operatorname{HeegnerHypothesis}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(K,N)\n\\land\\operatorname{Order}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\mathcal O,K)\\\\\n&\\land\\gcd(N,[\\mathcal O_K:\\mathcal O])=1\n\\land\\operatorname{ModularParametrization}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\varphi,X_0(N),E,O)\\\\\n&\\land\\operatorname{CMPoint}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(x,X_0(N),\\mathcal O)\n\\land P=\\varphi(x)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}heegner\\text{-}point\\text{-}existential}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\operatorname{HeegnerPoint}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(P,E,K)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists N,\\mathcal O,\\varphi,x\\;\\operatorname{HeegnerPointData}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(P,E,K,N,\\mathcal O,\\varphi,x).","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}heegner\\text{-}point\\text{-}compatibility}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\mathrm{HeegnerPoint}_S(P,E,K)\n\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{HeegnerPoint}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(P,E,K).","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathbb Q","display":false},{"tex":"X_0(N)","display":false},{"tex":"L'(E/K,1)","display":false},{"tex":"L'(E, 1)","display":false},{"tex":"\\to","display":false}],"bytes":3583,"backlinks":[{"id":"ea1eda7a3ad5e5c0","anchor":"ref-1","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-613","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch03/58-df-heegner-point.md|58-df-heegner-point]]（batch03）"}],"outgoing":["74f4744df7db749f","e1616e874e8eb33c"]}